  THIS REPOSITORY IS A FORK OF MATIEC

 This is a fork of beremiz/matiec (https://github.com/beremiz/matiec), maintained by AlexIII.
It lives at https://github.com/AlexIII/matiec and branches from upstream beremiz/default at commit 97d311d.
The version is kept in the VERSION file (e.g. 0.1-alexiii.2); "iec2c -v" prints the version and the git commit.
To build, see README.build (Docker builds for Windows and Linux). The original upstream readme follows the
separator below.

 What this fork adds over upstream:

 New features / language extensions (all off by default, existing programs compile unchanged)
 - STRING[n]: per-variable, function block field and struct field string widths (storage of n+1 bytes
   instead of 127); out-of-range widths and unsupported contexts are diagnosed (bb7f7ff)
 - -X_ENUM_TO_INT: implicit enumerated value to integer conversion in assignments, FB inputs and
   function parameters (b55621b, 25a58a8)
 - -X_INT_TO_REAL: implicit integer to REAL/LREAL conversion for decimal literals and integer variables of
   2 bytes or less; REAL-typed literals are emitted as x.0 in C (25a58a8)
 - VARIABLES.csv: struct-typed variables are listed as one row per leaf field with the full dotted path,
   including bounded STRING[n] fields (46fc1bc)

 Bug fixes
 - Accept bytes 0x80-0xFF in ST string literals; string literal length is now taken from sizeof() so it
   matches the emitted bytes (df5a8b1)
 - Fix C code generation for array function parameters (e8824e4)
 - Fix segfault in VARIABLES.csv generation for comma-listed FB instances and structs ("a, b, c : TON") (ca5022b)
 - Fix gcc warning (misleading indentation) in the IL function call generator (642596a)
 - Fix missing semicolon in AnnexF/delay_st.txt (cbe6ad5)
 - Runtime: __iec_error() now calls exit(0x102) instead of printing to stderr (03de001)

 Fixes cherry-picked from other forks/authors
 - Struct initializer bound to the wrong member: find_element() used an ordering functor as an equality test
   (Edouard Tisserant, beremiz c1df93e; 5a78964)
 - RETAIN qualifier lost after the first global in a VAR_GLOBAL RETAIN block (Edouard Tisserant, beremiz
   12e4828; ba0f857)
 - Crash when an enum value is used in a struct/array initializer (Edouard Tisserant, beremiz f7185c6; 6401fa9)
 - Initialization of arrays of non-simple types, required by the fix below (Edouard Tisserant, beremiz
   5b9968b; c1ffc9a)
 - Internal compiler error when an array initializer has too many elements; now a stage 3 error (Edouard
   Tisserant, beremiz c73c55d; a24363d)
 - F_TRIG first-cycle output: internal memory initialised to TRUE so Q is not spuriously set; also applied to
   the no_ENENO variant (Thiago Alves, thiagoralves/matiec f-trigger-fix, b082b44 and b3df950; 11b2208, 89e5558)

 Build & tooling
 - Version comes from the VERSION file; -v prints version and git commit (replaces the Mercurial changeset id) (42931eb)
 - Docker builds: Windows cross-compile (iec2c.exe) and native Linux (iec2c) into ./dist/ (fba496a, 42931eb, eb395d9)
 - Regression tests: tests/upstream_fixes, tests/var_list, tests/string_widths (84f36c9, 76cf5ed, 46fc1bc,
   ca5022b, bb7f7ff)
 - Documentation: UPSTREAM_MERGE_NOTES.md (upstream commits reviewed and merged), KNOWN_ISSUES.md
   (1a649a7, 54b4ec1, b7e7732)

